  "description": "JEZRIT crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C64 H120 Ce6 N16 O48. From the CIF bond table, Ce1 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce2 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce3 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce4 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce5 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce6 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.746-3.787 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 100.76-118.01°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Ce6IV(O)4(OH)4(H2O)8(DOTAH)4]. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 8 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 8 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
